# eEyes shells (Android + Desktop)

Canonical product contract: [`docs/specs/010-eeyes.md`](../../docs/specs/010-eeyes.md).

## Parity rule

Implement the **same behavior** in `android/` (Kotlin) and `desktop/` (WPF .NET 8) in the **same turn**. Do not ship a feature on one platform without the other unless the user explicitly scopes one side.

Shared:

- Bridge message types and payloads
- Allowlisted device API paths
- Media compression rules (JPEG q70 max edge 1600; AAC-LC mono 64 kbps M4A)
- Offline upload queue + exponential backoff
- Token lifetime handling (`device_revoked` / `device_expired` → clear + re-pair)
- Sync loop (~30s) and notification scheduling from task `notifyAt` / reminders
- Update check against `latest.json` + sha256 verify

Platform-only APIs (camera, secure storage, FGS vs tray) may differ; behavior must match.

## Shell responsibilities only

Token storage, WebView host, bridge, sync, local notifications, photo, audio, compress+base64+queue, apply updates. **No** product UI chrome beyond what `/api/eeyes/ui` provides.

## Security

- Token never enters WebView JS.
- Origin allowlist: production `https://eduardoos.com` (local override via build config).
- Navigation locked to `/api/eeyes/ui*`; other URLs → system browser.
- Capture only while a human-started task is `in_progress`, with a visible indicator.

## UI source of truth

HTML/CSS/JS lives in `backend/eeyes_ui/` and is served by the Go API. Edit there to update both apps without a shell release when only UI changes. Shell version bumps are for native capability / update pipeline only.
